<title>USA: TABLE - Homegate Hospitality Q2 full results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Homegate Hospitality Q2 full results.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Mos Ended	   Six Mos Ended</p>
<p>				   Jun 30, 1997	    Jun 30, 1997</p>
<p>Revenue</p>
<p>	   Room revenue	  $2,105,812		$4,021,929</p>
<p>	   Other revenue	     45,662		   103,393</p>
<p>	   Interest Income	  221,603		   603,218</p>
<p> Total revenue		    2,373,077		 4,728,540</p>
<p>Costs and expenses</p>
<p>Property operating expenses</p>
<p>					1,421,580		 2,709,680</p>
<p>Corporate operating expenses</p>
<p>					  628,132		 1,415,755</p>
<p>Depreciation and amortization</p>
<p>					  354,468		   623,498</p>
<p>   Interest			   395,628		   880,145</p>
<p> Total costs and expenses     2,799,808		 5,629,078</p>
<p> Net loss			   (426,731)		 (900,538)</p>
<p> Net loss per share		   (.04)		     (.08)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p> shares outstanding	    10,725,000		10,725,000</p>
<p>NOTES: On July 25, 1997, Homegate announced a definitive merger agreement with Prime Hospitality Corp. Prime Hospitality will issue 0.6073 of a share of its common stock for each of the about 10.7 million outstanding shares of Homegate.</p>
<p>The company's full name is Homegate Hospitality Inc. Comparative figures for the year-earlier periods were not immediately available.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
